    "dynamicPruningFalsifier": "At size20 dynamic K1 scored 6/8 and at size100 10/12. In both matrices wrongToolSelection occurred iff the correct target was hidden from the first turn; Swift software was replaced by swift-bird and Rust software by corrosion. K4 kept the correct candidate visible and all tasks passed.",
    "largeStaticFalsifier": "100-tool static surface remained 12/12 correct. It used 155055 prompt tokens, but 140800 were cache hits and 14255 misses. Therefore tool count or total prompt alone does not imply deferred discovery.",
    "deferredTradeoff": "100-tool deferred was 12/12 with only 21058 prompt tokens but 24 Provider calls versus static 12, 12226 cache-miss tokens versus static 14255, and higher measured latency. Deferred is a strategy trade, not a universal replacement.",
    "genericSimplicityControl": "generic catalog remained correct at sizes 5/20/100. This is evidence that a simpler surface is a serious baseline, not evidence to replace typed tools universally."
